---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import HeroText from "../components/HeroText.astro";

const metadata = {
  siteTitle: "Seaside Heritage Network",
  pageTitle: "Privacy Policy",
  description:
    "How the Seaside Heritage Network collects, uses and looks after your personal information.",
};

const lastUpdated = "2026-09-26";
const lastUpdatedLabel = "26 September 2026";

const proseClass =
  "prose prose-headings:font-heading prose-headings:font-medium prose-h2:text-3xl prose-h2:text-[var(--shn-color-bg-page)] prose-h2:scroll-mt-24 prose-p:text-gray-700 prose-li:text-gray-700 prose-ul:list-disc prose-ul:list-outside prose-ul:pl-5 [&_li::marker]:text-gray-700 prose-a:text-[var(--shn-color-primary)] prose-a:underline-offset-2 hover:prose-a:text-accent max-w-3xl";
---

<PageLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <HeroText
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle="How the Seaside Heritage Network collects, uses and looks after your personal information."
  />

  <section class="bg-stone-100 text-dark">
    <div
      class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:flex lg:justify-center"
    >
      <article class={proseClass}>
        <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          The Seaside Heritage Network is a charity (registered as a Foundation
          CIO with the Charity Commission for England and Wales, charity number
          1216037) that raises awareness and understanding of the heritage
          associated with the UK seaside holiday.
        </p>
        <p>
          For the purposes of data protection law, the Seaside Heritage Network
          is the "data controller" of the personal information described in this
          policy. If you have any questions about this policy or how we handle
          your data, you can contact us using the details at the bottom of this
          page.
        </p>

        <h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          We collect very little personal information, and only when you choose
          to give it to us:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Newsletter sign-up:</strong> if you subscribe to our newsletter,
            we collect your email address (and name, if you give it) through Brevo,
            the email platform we use to send it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Event bookings:</strong> bookings for our events are handled by
            TicketSource, which collects your name, email address and booking details.
            If you choose to join our mailing list when booking, we add your email
            address to our newsletter in Brevo.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Getting in touch:</strong> if you email us, we'll see your email
            address and whatever you choose to tell us in your message.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Website visits:</strong> our website host keeps standard server
            logs, which include your IP address, to keep the site secure and working
            properly. See "Cookies and analytics" below for how we measure visits.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We don't ask visitors to create an account, and there's nowhere on the
          site to leave public comments.
        </p>

        <h2 id="lawful-basis">Lawful basis</h2>
        <p>
          Under UK data protection law, we rely on the following grounds to use
          your information:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Consent</strong> – for sending you our newsletter, including if
            you opt in when booking an event. You can withdraw this at any time by
            unsubscribing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contract</strong> – for processing your event booking.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legitimate interests</strong> – for replying to enquiries you
            send us, and for keeping the website running securely.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="cookies-and-analytics">Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>Our website doesn't set any cookies of its own.</p>
        <p>
          We use <a href="https://plausible.io/" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Plausible Analytics</a
          >, a privacy-friendly analytics tool, to understand how people use our
          site. Plausible doesn't use cookies and doesn't store any personal
          information – it only records anonymous, aggregated statistics such as
          page views, how people found the site, and which country they're
          visiting from. No individual visitor can be identified from this data.
          You can read more in{" "}
          <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Plausible's data policy</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          Video content from YouTube on our Resource Hub is shown as a static
          thumbnail – nothing is loaded from YouTube until you press play. Once
          you do, the video loads in "privacy-enhanced mode" (via
          youtube-nocookie.com), which reduces, but doesn't fully eliminate, the
          cookies Google may set. You can read more in{" "}
          <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          If we ever add anything else that sets cookies, we'll update this page
          and ask for your consent first.
        </p>

        <h2 id="who-we-share-with">Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          We don't sell or rent your personal information. We only share it with
          the organisations that help us run the services below:
        </p>
        <dl class="not-prose text-gray-700">
          <div
            class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr] gap-x-5 py-3.5 border-b border-stone-300"
          >
            <dt class="font-semibold text-(--shn-color-bg-page)">Brevo</dt>
            <dd>Sends our email newsletter to subscribers.</dd>
          </div>
          <div
            class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr] gap-x-5 py-3.5 border-b border-stone-300"
          >
            <dt class="font-semibold text-(--shn-color-bg-page)">
              TicketSource
            </dt>
            <dd>Handles event bookings.</dd>
          </div>
          <div
            class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr] gap-x-5 py-3.5 border-b border-stone-300"
          >
            <dt class="font-semibold text-(--shn-color-bg-page)">Netlify</dt>
            <dd>Hosts our website.</dd>
          </div>
          <div
            class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr] gap-x-5 py-3.5 border-b border-stone-300"
          >
            <dt class="font-semibold text-(--shn-color-bg-page)">123 Reg</dt>
            <dd>Hosts our email.</dd>
          </div>
          <div
            class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr] gap-x-5 py-3.5 border-b border-stone-300"
          >
            <dt class="font-semibold text-(--shn-color-bg-page)">Plausible</dt>
            <dd>Provides anonymous, cookie-free website analytics.</dd>
          </div>
          <div
            class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[160px_1fr] gap-x-5 py-3.5 border-b border-stone-300"
          >
            <dt class="font-semibold text-(--shn-color-bg-page)">
              YouTube (Google)
            </dt>
            <dd>Hosts our videos, only when you choose to play one.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p>
          We may also need to share information if required to do so by law.
        </p>

        <h2 id="international-transfers">International transfers</h2>
        <p>
          Some of the services we use are based, or store data, outside the UK.
          Where this happens, we rely on providers that protect your information
          to UK standards, for example through the UK's adequacy regulations or
          the UK International Data Transfer Agreement.
        </p>

        <h2 id="how-long-we-keep-it">How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Newsletter:</strong> we keep your details in Brevo for as long
            as you stay subscribed. If you unsubscribe, your email address is kept
            on a suppression list so we don't email you again by mistake.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Event bookings:</strong> TicketSource keeps booking records under{
              " "
            }
            <a
              href="https://www.ticketsource.com/kb/terms-of-use/customer-data-privacy-policy"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">its own privacy policy</a
            >.{" "}
            <mark class="bg-pink-100 text-accent px-1 rounded not-prose">
              [Confirm how long SHN keeps attendee lists after an event.]
            </mark>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Enquiries:</strong> we keep emails only for as long as needed
            to deal with your enquiry and any necessary follow-up.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under UK data protection law, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            ask us what personal information we hold about you, and get a copy
            of it
          </li>
          <li>ask us to correct information that's inaccurate or incomplete</li>
          <li>ask us to delete your information</li>
          <li>ask us to restrict how we use your information</li>
          <li>object to us using your information</li>
          <li>withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on consent</li>
          <li>
            ask for your information to be moved to another organisation, where
            technically possible
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details below.
          If you're not happy with how we've handled your information, you also
          have the right to complain to the{" "}
          <a
            href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a
          >, the UK's data protection regulator.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We review this policy regularly. When we change it, we'll update the
          date below.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy was last updated on{" "}
          <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{lastUpdatedLabel}</time>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">How to contact us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions about this policy or how we use your
          information, email us at{" "}
          <a href="mailto:info@seasideheritage.org.uk">
            info@seasideheritage.org.uk
          </a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
